WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.520
Something really strange is happening&nbsp;
at White House press briefings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.720
lately. It's almost like reporters&nbsp;
don't have any idea what to ask about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.600
And I don't want to suggest that there is nothing&nbsp;
to ask about. As I've talked about for weeks now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:19.600
Joe Biden's failed executive order on stopping&nbsp;
deportations, foreign policy questions, minimum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:25.040
wage. There are plenty of things to ask about&nbsp;
during Jen Psaki White House press briefings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:30.160
But for some reason, reporters at press&nbsp;
briefings are increasingly concerned with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.800
asking over and over and over again, why&nbsp;
won't you call the situation at the border&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:41.360
a crisis which is just this endlessly semantic&nbsp;
question? And yesterday, questions about Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:50.480
Biden's dogs and possibly a cat. I'm not joking,&nbsp;
Joe Biden's younger dog, Major Biden, bit someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:56.240
at the White House, the person is fine. As of&nbsp;
yesterday, it wasn't totally clear who it was.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.640
As of today, it seems that it was a Secret&nbsp;
Service agent. It was reported that Major Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.640
was sort of surprised as a Secret Service agent&nbsp;
came around the corner or something like that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.360
had a minor injury treated at the White House&nbsp;
now after one reporter had already asked about it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:17.200
yesterday. Another reporter asks a follow up and&nbsp;
the question is phrased in a wacky, histrionic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:24.720
dramatic way, asking whether Jen Psaki can assure&nbsp;
the American public that Major Biden isn't going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.440
to be euthanized. Look at this about three things.
That's a state that, of course, dogs immigration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:34.160
And then, Governor, another dog's question. OK,&nbsp;
go ahead to follow. Just a quick clarification&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.000
on the dogs. OK, can you confirm that it&nbsp;
was a Secret Service member who was bitten?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.720
And can you also reassure the public that Mr.&nbsp;
Biden will not be euthanized as a result of this?&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:47.840
Well, certainly, Major Biden is a member of the&nbsp;
family. So I can assure you that I don't have any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.240
more details on the individual. I would encourage&nbsp;
you to ask the Secret Service, but I'm not going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:58.400
to have any more intimate details other than that.
It's all phrased in the most histrionic and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:05.040
dramatic terms possible. Jen, can you assure the&nbsp;
public as if the public is waiting around to know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:12.720
this, that major won't be euthanized? If you have&nbsp;
to ask a second question about Joe Biden's dogs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.160
maybe it would be has the Biden family determined&nbsp;
how they will handle Major Biden in the future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.160
in light of this dog bite? Like if you if you&nbsp;
are going to insist on asking more about it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.760
But can you reassure us he won't be euthanized,&nbsp;
just desperate to create controversy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:33.520
if she had said I have no idea whether they're&nbsp;
going to euthanize the dog. I haven't spoken to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:39.200
Joe Biden about it than the headline would&nbsp;
be. Jen Psaki refuses to deny that, Joe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.560
that Major Biden might be euthanized. And then I&nbsp;
guess at some point someone in the past said maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:51.120
the Bidens will be getting a cat. And another&nbsp;
reporter asking about the cat, if you can imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.440
questions we had about dogs, we were promised&nbsp;
the White House cat what happened to that?&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.080
Where is the cat today? A good day for the&nbsp;
cat. I don't have any update on the cat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.920
We know the cat will break the Internet,&nbsp;
but I don't have any update on its status.&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:11.280
So there it is literally devolving into questions&nbsp;
about dogs and cats. And I think part of what's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.640
going on here part is the reporters don't&nbsp;
don't know what to ask about substantively.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:23.120
Part of it is that we are now moving beyond the&nbsp;
reality TV presidency of Donald Trump. Joe Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:28.240
isn't tweeting attacks at people all day long. Joe&nbsp;
Biden's administration is denouncing the press as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:34.400
an institution. And it's sort of like reporters&nbsp;
are struggling to move beyond the reality show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:41.440
that was the Trump presidency. My question to you&nbsp;
is, do you think they don't know what to ask or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:47.520
do they think that these questions will be seen as&nbsp;
relevant and interesting by the American people? I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:52.320
just don't even understand the motivation to ask&nbsp;
about a cat. Maybe don't ask a question if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.400
have nothing relevant to ask about. Maybe that's&nbsp;
part of it. Where if you're in the briefing room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:02.000
even if you have nothing to say, you want to get&nbsp;
a question in there. And so you ask about a cat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.880
I really don't have the explanation as to what's&nbsp;
going on, but I'd be curious to hear from you.&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:13.547
And we'll have more on this on The David Pakman&nbsp;
Show Instagram page. Find us on Instagram at David&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.547 --> 00:05:30.104
Pakman show. Find me on Instagram at David Pakman.&nbsp;
The David Pakman Show at David Pakman dot com.

